-- title:
--   Original BV positive-shift pathwise stopped cash dominated by its actual intrinsic compensated source
-- statement:
--   For the same original BV Levy process and admissible strategy, strict original cash plus surviving pre-right-payment shifted terminal is pathwise bounded almost surely by the shifted initial value plus the explicitly defined compensated integral of the actual original jump-counting measure NX. Its predictable integrand uses the original bounded ruin clock and a deterministic compact band of the shifted left reserve. This contains no expectation or martingale assumption. It isolates the actual discounted BV chain inequality with the original mixed source/dividend chronology. Proof plan in positive-shift-chain-proof.md: use original X=d*t-J, gradient/secant dividend signs, actual jump chain rule, and discard the nonpositive original physical HJB time integral; handle tau=0 and the pre-right-payment endpoint separately. Parent positive-shift expectation 0d51b191 follows by Proved genuine NX compensation 7cf52fcc and Proved shifted payoff L1 f3680361. This is a proposed child only; no current graph edge or proof acceptance is claimed.

